# ComfyUI-TrajectoryForcing
#
# Its own repo (a submodule of msc-thesis), so these rules stand alone rather
# than leaning on the parent's .gitignore.

# Run outputs, on the same pattern as TrajectoryDreamer/outputs (see the parent
# repo's CLAUDE.md): anything a run produces lives beside the code that made it,
# and is never committed.
# (Listed as /outputs/* rather than /outputs/ so the re-include below can reach
# inside: git will not descend into an excluded directory to un-exclude a file.)
/outputs/*
# ...except the Slurm log directory itself: #SBATCH --output= will not create it,
# and the job fails at launch when it is missing.
!/outputs/slurm_logs/
/outputs/slurm_logs/*
!/outputs/slurm_logs/.gitkeep

# Checkpoints and model weights are multi-GB and belong outside git -- the plan
# is to symlink them from TrajectoryForcing/checkpoints rather than copy them.
/checkpoints/
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.npz

# The working record: design history, job ids, what each run found. Kept
# locally and deliberately not published, so nothing in the repo may link to it.
/PLAN.md

# ComfyUI drops these into a custom-node directory at runtime.
/web/extensions/**/dist/
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# Test / type / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Environments -- ComfyUI's own venv lives outside this repo entirely, so the
# usual `env/` rule is not needed and would swallow env/setup.sh, which is the
# tracked script that builds it (same convention as TrajectoryDreamer/env/).
.venv
venv/
ENV/
# .env is your machine's paths: `cp .env.example .env`. Every script sources it
# if present, and keeping it untracked is what lets the committed defaults stay
# generic. .env.example is the tracked template and is not matched by this rule.
.env
.envrc

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.tmp

# Left by install.py when it declines to touch the environment; read back at
# startup by tf_nodes/health.py. Per-install state, never committed.
/SETUP-REQUIRED.txt
